\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Thou great Redeemer, dying Lamb,
\par We love to hear of Thee;
\par No music's like Thy charming name,
\par Nor half so sweet can be.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Our Jesus shall be still our theme
\par While in this world we stay:
\par We'll sing our Jesu's lovely name
\par When all things else decay.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. When we appear in yonder cloud,
\par With all that favoured throng,
\par Then will we sing more sweet, more loud,
\par And Christ shall be our song.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

